        "answer": {
          "short": "People Infected, Days 3–5: $2\\times2\\times2$; $2\\times2\\times2\\times2$; $2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times2$.\nIndex Notation, Days 0–5: $2^0$, $2^1$, $2^2$, $2^3$, $2^4$, $2^5$.",
          "worked": "Each new day adds one factor of $2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\times2\\times2&=2^3\\\\2\\times2\\times2\\times2&=2^4\\\\2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times2&=2^5\\end{align*}$$\nFor Days 0–5, the index-notation entries are $2^0$, $2^1$, $2^2$, $2^3$, $2^4$, $2^5$. Day 0 has one infected person, so $2^0=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
